=== what this run says ===

  baseline                                          ALIVE
  after ONE fire at 0x300a                          ALIVE
  phase 1  read all 128 ArduChip registers, 3 times, NO fires ALIVE
  phase 2  36 writes of 0x07 = 0x00, no bits set    ALIVE
  phase 3  fire at the FIVE HIGH addresses, 3 visits (0x3000-0x3100) ALIVE
  phase 4  fire at the SEVEN LOW addresses, 3 visits (0x0000-0x001D) ALIVE

  NOTHING IN 20260907-i2cpass's STAGE A BREAKS THE HANDLE when it is done
  a piece at a time - not the dump, not writing 0x07, not the high
  addresses, not the low ones. Whatever cost that probe its control
  surface needs the pieces STACKED, and the next run should stop
  bisecting and instead re-run stage A whole with a handle check
  before it as well as after.
